// EN translation FIRST PASS. Literary editorial approval outstanding.
const OUTCOMES_EN_E151_E220 = Object.freeze({"E151.1":{"s":"Taar lowers the cradle onto the stone, and the knocking under the shell finally subsides; the keeper silently hands you travel supplies.","f":"A knock answers from deep inside the cave. Armed guardians of the clutch emerge from the darkness, and the conversation turns into a skirmish."},"E151.2":{"s":"Taar takes the cradle away from the cracks, although the egg continues to dully tap on his back for a long time. For your help, the keeper gives you gold.","f":"The egg begins to beat against the bars of the cradle so hard that the party has to stop and spend supplies for a break."},"E151.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} listens to the pauses between blows and finds a trace of alien magic stretching from the cave. Taar pays for the solution of the mystery in gold.","f":"{{heroName}} distinguishes someone else's voice in the knocking, but the source remains hidden. Taar takes the cradle and leaves without answering."},"E151.4":{"s":"The shell splits, and an indignant voice announces, quite clearly, “I said back, not out!” Taar stares at you, apparently at a loss for words.","f":"Your first blow against the shell wakes the creatures guarding the clutch deep inside the mountain. An entire hostile warband emerges from the cave. A battle begins."},"E151.5":{"s":"You leave Taar alone with his unusual cargo. Already around the turn, a short, distinct voice is heard from behind: “Back.”"},"E152.1":{"s":"The alchemical composition gives Kerr a steady flame instead of a pathetic cloud of smoke. Nima smiles for the first time, and Kerr thanks the party with gold.","f":"The composition produces only a loud bang and thick smoke; Nima is forced to extinguish the edge of the squire's cloak. Kerr decides not to repeat the experiment."},"E152.2":{"s":"Kerr removes the ceremonial sign and speaks for the first time about his victories without mentioning the flame. Nima gives the party some provisions for their help.","f":"Kerr listens to the arguments and still adjusts the straps of the ceremonial spear. He intends to go to the ritual, even if he can only exhale smoke again."},"E152.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} arranges a duel where the accuracy of the spear and endurance are decided; Kerr wins without a spark. The squire gives you the due reward.","f":"The audience demands fire, not wanting to evaluate Kerr's skill. {{heroName}} stops the test before the ridicule becomes insults."},"E152.4":{"s":"Kerr looks at the spear for a long time, then agrees that real strength is proven on the road, not on the platform. A new companion joins your party.","f":"Kerr thanks for the offer, but remains to wait for tomorrow's ceremony. Nima follows you with a long, anxious look.","v":{"rs":"Kerr is ready to prove himself on the road, but there is no room for him in your party. He gives you gold in thanks for the invitation."}},"E152.5":{"s":"You leave Kerr practising with his spear by the roadside. Behind you comes another cough, followed by a stubborn “One more time.”"},"E153.1":{"s":"Sarah is indignant at first, but the old coppers still turn into a common dinner instead of another page of the legend. They are collecting supplies for your journey."},"E153.2":{"s":"Collectors suddenly start bidding for ancient coppers, and Sarah sees real value in the chest for the first time. After the deal, the party gets gold.","f":"Sarah names a price of such antiquity that even you lose the desire to argue. The chest remains under guard, and the money invested in negotiations cannot be returned."},"E153.3":{"s":"The note is put on display next to the chest; There are surprisingly many people willing to buy a four-hundred-year-old joke. The proceeds replenish the treasury.","f":"Buyers consider the note to be a fake, and the auction collapses with a loud scandal. To settle the claims, the party loses some of the gold."},"E153.4":{"s":"Sarah studies the magnificent emptiness of the chest, then asks for help inventorying the locked treasury. She rewards your frankness with a modest sum of gold."},"E153.5":{"s":"You leave Sarah, the guards and the copper coins alone with four centuries of service zeal. Outside they are already arguing about who should be put in charge of guarding the note."},"E154.1":{"s":"Tessa puts the scales into the coals and for the first time all evening stops arguing with her brother. After the burial, relatives share provisions with you."},"E154.2":{"s":"Wark carefully wraps the scales in linen; Tessa turns away, but doesn't try to stop him. For support, the family donates gold to the party."},"E154.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} suggests leaving a carved copy of the scales next to the ashes, and keeping the original for the children. Brother and sister accept the ceremony and thank you with gold and supplies.","f":"{{heroName}}'s suggestion strikes both mourners as too cold a farewell. The coals burn low while their quarrel continues."},"E154.4":{"s":"You divide the scales and give half to each; For the first time that evening, Wark and Tessa find words that don’t sound like reproach.","f":"The edges of the golden scales crumble under the tool, and both heirs stop you in horror. Still no solution."},"E154.5":{"s":"You leave rather than decide what matters more to the family: remembrance or farewell. Behind you, Tessa puts another coal on the fire."},"E155.1":{"s":"The seal is found in Fek's inkwell, where he himself dropped it. The groom lowers his shoulders for the first time in a day and a half, and the clerk counts out your reward.","f":"Fek turns over all the boxes, but there is no seal anywhere. The groom remains at his post, and your people spend provisions helping with the search."},"E155.2":{"s":"At the King's order, Grum finally removes his helmet and hands the watch over to his relief. The grateful guard shares provisions.","f":"Grum points to the blank space reserved for the seal. “Orders are accepted after registration.” His exhaustion has clearly outlasted common sense."},"E155.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} transfers the guard's assignment directly to the barracks door without formally breaking a single regulation. Grum can finally sleep, and your party receives supplies.","f":"{{heroName}} finds a loophole, but Fek demands three more confirmation signatures. The groom stands there in his armor, almost without blinking."},"E155.4":{"s":"You give Fek a fresh seal, and the long-awaited impression appears on the papers. The clerk pays for the work while Grum collapses onto a bench."},"E155.5":{"s":"You leave Grum at the gate with his regulations and his miserable shift. As you depart, the rhinoceros asks just one thing: “If you find the seal, come back.”"},"E156.1":{"s":"Raven pales as Mara reads his footprints aloud at the counter. The stolen goods turn up in the lining of his bag, and the herbalist pays you in gold.","f":"The official demands an apology for the public accusation, and the case ends with a fine. Mara hisses with displeasure, but cannot compensate for the losses of the party."},"E156.2":{"s":"You follow the path of all three, and the tracks lead to a hidden cache behind the bench. Mara returns the seeds and shares the travel supplies.","f":"The traces disappear among street vendors, and no one is able to prove the theft. Mara closes the shop earlier than usual."},"E156.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} notices how the raven involuntarily covers one sleeve with each question from Mara. The seeds are found, and the herbalist rewards observation with gold.","f":"The raven, the hare and the badger are equally convincingly indignant at the interrogation; even {{heroName}} can’t catch anyone in a lie."},"E156.4":{"s":"You pay for Mara's loss, and she finally puts off asking questions until tomorrow. The herbalist collects some provisions for you on the way."},"E156.5":{"s":"You leave the store, leaving three customers in front of Mara and her small cat. The cat does not leave the raven's boot."},"E157.1":{"s":"Rakh begins quietly, but the council gradually stops whispering and listens to the meaning of his words. Saara thanks you with a small supply of provisions.","f":"The first burst of laughter silences Rakh before he can finish his introduction. Saara embraces her son, but he has failed to win over the council."},"E157.2":{"s":"The alien roar behind the curtain is triggered, and the council listens to Rakh’s speech to the end. Saara pays in gold, although Rakh himself keeps looking at the floor.","f":"Behind the curtain, someone coughs ahead of schedule, and the substitution becomes obvious. Rakh leaves the platform before the first accusation is made."},"E157.3":{"s":"Instead of roaring, Rakh asks the council a question none of the elders can answer. Saara rewards your help with provisions.","f":"The elders interrupt the first question with a demand to observe custom. Rakh is forced to retreat without starting his speech."},"E157.4":{"s":"Rakh advances in front of your party, gets lost in the middle, but still starts over. In parting, he thanks for the opportunity to make mistakes without ridicule."},"E157.5":{"s":"You leave Rakh to face his trial alone. As you depart, the young lion is still rehearsing the first word of his speech."},"E158.1":{"s":"The builders remove the stones one by one, while Hadar silently watches from the side of the road. Engineers pay in gold for the solution that made the road safer.","f":"Hadar gets in the way of the workers, and a calm conversation turns into a dangerous brawl. There's a skirmish ahead."},"E158.2":{"s":"Work stops. Hadar settles beside the old parapet and touches the stone gratefully with his trunk. The builders share supplies, though the bridge still needs repairs."},"E158.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} proposes to preserve the old stones in the supports of the new bridge. Hadar finally clears the road, and the engineers reward the solution with gold.","f":"{{heroName}} shows calculations, but engineers are not ready to vouch for the strength of the structure. Hadar remains on the bridge, but the work stops."},"E158.4":{"s":"Hadar carefully takes a stone from the old masonry with his trunk and steps aside. As a reminder of your help, the workers supply you with provisions.","f":"Hadar responds with a quiet refusal: for him, one stone cannot replace an entire bridge. Work remains suspended."},"E158.5":{"s":"You leave without deciding how to weigh someone else's memory against the danger of a future flood. Hadar still lies across the road."},"E159.1":{"s":"Ren tries to hide the scroll, but the travelers are already demanding the return of the illegal fee. Some of the confiscated coins end up in your treasury.","f":"Ren rips the tablecloth off the table and gives the signal to his men. A dubious tax has to be challenged with weapons - a skirmish begins."},"E159.2":{"s":"Ren returns the coins to the travelers amid dissatisfied murmurs; They share supplies with the party for help. The fox promises to study the law “much more narrowly” in the future.","f":"Ren suddenly demands three copies of every refund request, each with witnesses. The exhausted travellers disperse empty-handed."},"E159.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} finds the actual law against unlawful tolls and reads it aloud. For once, Ren pays his fine in gold without trying to stretch the wording.","f":"Ren states that the matter falls under the jurisdiction of a completely different forest. {{heroName}} ends the dispute: it is impossible to prove the forgery today."},"E159.4":{"s":"Ren offers you a share, and you do not interfere with his trade with someone else's confusion. Gold is added to the treasury, but the line of travelers does not decrease."},"E159.5":{"s":"You drive past a table with a ridiculous tax. Ren already explains to the next traveler that there is an additional payment for moral unpreparedness."},"E160.1":{"s":"You bury the stranger with his medallion. Kesh silently watches the fresh soil and leaves before dawn."},"E160.2":{"s":"Kesh performs the rites of his people, taking care not to mock another's grief. In farewell, the hyena leaves provisions for the party."},"E160.3":{"s":"You keep the medallion in case the dead man's kin come looking, and Kesh gains permission to perform his rites. The hyena rewards your trust with supplies."},"E160.4":{"s":"You leave before dawn. Kesh remains motionless beside the road."},"E160.5":{"s":"Kesh dodges the first blow and answers with unexpected fury. A purse of coins lies nearby, but the conversation is over: a skirmish begins."},"E161.1":{"s":"The golem carefully lowers the block to the ground, then sits down and for the first time in sixty-three years does nothing. Master Kohl rereads the instructions in complete silence."},"E161.2":{"s":"On a direct order, the golem takes a few more steps with the stone, and Master Kohl counts out the payment. The \"BREAK: 0\" message does not disappear.","f":"No. 18 places a block across the road and repeats: “I WANT TO SIT.” In search of a detour, the party has to use up supplies."},"E161.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} adds compulsory breaks to the work cycle. For the first time, Golem No. 18 agrees to lift the stone without protest. Kohl rewards the solution with gold and provisions.","f":"{{heroName}} finds the right command, but the golem claims that the pauses should have started sixty-three years ago. The mechanism does not move."},"E161.4":{"s":"Kol accepts payment for #18, and the golem carefully rises from its first rest. A new companion appears in your party.","f":"Kohl refuses to let No. 18 go, even after receiving the money offered. The golem settles down in the middle of the road and no longer listens to orders.","v":{"rs":"Golem No. 18 accepts the assignment, but there is no place for him in your party. Kohl gives you gold in thanks."}},"E161.5":{"s":"The party squeezes along the side of the road, going around the boulder. Golem #18 then says, “HAVE A NICE BREAK.”"},"E162.1":{"s":"Lem finds the automaton guilty along with his disobedient hand and closes the case. For your help with the investigation, he gives you gold."},"E162.2":{"s":"Inside the removed hand, a separate chain of commands is discovered, leading to someone else's order. Lem rewards the find with gold.","f":"As soon as you touch the fastenings, S-4's left hand fights back, and the other automata rush to its aid. A skirmish begins."},"E162.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} restores the command log and shows Lem who forced the hand to take the key. The interrogator counts out the promised reward.","f":"{{heroName}} finds a memory break, but the reason is unclear even after checking again. Lem postpones the sentence."},"E162.4":{"s":"S-4 is declared faulty, and after payment it comes under your banner as a new companion. The left hand is kept in sight the entire way.","f":"Lem refuses to sell the automaton until the end of the investigation. S-4 hides his left hand behind his back as if it means nothing.","v":{"rs":"S-4 is willing to leave the workshop, but your party has no room for another fighter. Lem offers gold instead of a sale."}},"E162.5":{"s":"You leave Lem to figure out who exactly is to blame: the whole S-4 or his left hand. The automaton quietly repeats that he did not take the key."},"E163.1":{"s":"Beck shows you where to brace the joints, and the walking tower halts behind the last house. The architect pays gold for saving the village.","f":"Stone legs crush the barriers, and the tower turns towards those who dared to stop it. There's a battle ahead."},"E163.2":{"s":"Residents manage to carry out their children and household belongings before the tower descends with a heavy thud on the outskirts. Beck admits that the view from here is truly excellent."},"E163.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} restores the signal marks of the old post, and the tower obediently returns in its own tracks. Bek gives you gold and supplies.","f":"{{heroName}} sets landmarks, but the tower considers the new coordinates even more promising and continues to move towards the village."},"E163.4":{"s":"The tower changes direction, seeing a more advantageous position near the enemy fortifications. Beck silently closes his eyes as dust rises over the hill.","f":"The tower recognizes your ruse as an attack and turns its guns on the party. A dispute with an ancient defensive machine turns into a battle."},"E163.5":{"s":"You leave Beck to run after his own structure. On the horizon, the tower confidently chooses a new hill."},"E164.1":{"s":"Lo stays before the charred door, clutching her mistress's ribbon against her chest. Even as you leave, you can hear her asking everyone to be quiet."},"E164.2":{"s":"The doll hears the truth, slowly lowers her wooden spear and lets you pass. You find surviving supplies among the ruins.","f":"At the news of her mistress's death, Lo's runes flare and her little spear grows terribly sharp. You must stop the house's defender in a skirmish."},"E164.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} politely asks Lo for permission to pass and promises that her order will not be forgotten. The doll leaves the doorway for the first time and becomes your companion.","f":"Lo answers {{heroName}} as quietly as before: “THE MISTRESS IS SLEEPING.” Her spear doesn't go down.","v":{"rs":"Lo is ready to leave the doorway for the first time, but your party has no room for her. The doll gives you gold for helping her understand her orders."}},"E164.4":{"s":"You remove the runes from the wooden frame, and the protective light finally goes out. Rare magic is paid in gold.","f":"The very first touch of the runes awakens all the protective spells of Lo. A burnt house suddenly becomes the site of a big battle."},"E164.5":{"s":"You slip around Lo through a gap in the wall and find valuables preserved among the ashes. The doll fails to notice, still guarding the doorway.","f":"An ancient seal ignites beneath the floorboards, and Lo blocks your path to the door. You cannot leave without fighting."},"E165.1":{"s":"The OR-7 mechanism takes the average time as official and removes the road blockade. The headman shares the supplies with relief.","f":"OR-7 declares the calculation invalid: “THE AVERAGE IS NOT THE EXACT.” The guardian automata remain at their posts."},"E165.2":{"s":"The guardian automata fall apart under your blows, and the roads reopen. The headman gives you a share of the town treasury.","f":"The first broken machine calls the others, and the area is filled with a metallic clang. A skirmish begins."},"E165.3":{"s":"By midnight, the stars give an exact time that OR-7 cannot challenge. The roads open, and the headman pays in gold for his patience."},"E165.4":{"s":"The royal herald proclaims noon, and OR-7 recognises the higher authority with obvious displeasure. The headman rewards you with gold.","f":"The clock answers the trumpet: “NOON WAS NOT CONFIRMED.” The royal decree turns out to be powerless in the face of stubborn gears."},"E165.5":{"s":"You choose a lane bypassing the square, leaving the headman to argue with the clock. The long hook takes up some of the supplies."},"E166.1":{"s":"M-9 holds both crystals in front of him for a long time, then asks Ella to begin the transfer. After the procedure, the master thanks you with gold, but still does not answer the philosophical question.","f":"Ella prepares a new crystal, but M-9 removes his hand at the last moment. Even all your arguments did not convince him to risk his own continuity."},"E166.2":{"s":"M-9 leaves his old crystal in place and asks Ella to write down how many days he has left. She rewards the careful decision with supplies."},"E166.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} performs a ritual linking the moment of the extinction of the old crystal with the launch of a new one. M-9 opens his eyes, says his name and thanks the party with gold.","f":"{{heroName}} notices a break in the ritual chain and does not dare to continue the transfer. M-9 is left alone with the same question."},"E166.4":{"s":"You pick up the old crystal after transfer, carefully placing it in the case. Ella warns that preserving memory does not mean preserving personality."},"E166.5":{"s":"You are not giving M-9 the answer for himself. He is left looking at two crystals, between which it is impossible to draw a simple line."},"E167.1":{"s":"The bear cannot withstand the roar of the shields and runs away, taking only its sticky paw. Dora shares the surviving supplies with the party.","f":"The bear responds to the noise with a blow of a huge paw; {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded. Dora goes back to the hives and doesn’t offer to make any more noise.","v":{"nf":"The bear protects the honey and drives away the noisemakers, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. Dora retreats to the hives."}},"E167.2":{"s":"The bear remains sitting with his barrel while the rest of the hives are carried over the fence. Dora allocates supplies, admitting that the compromise could be cheaper than a pitchfork."},"E167.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} sets up a feeding trough on the far edge of the forest, and the bear willingly changes the place of his visits. Dora pays in gold and gives out supplies.","f":"The bear does not trust the new feeder and again chooses the apiary. {{heroName}} is forced to retreat while the hives are still intact."},"E167.4":{"s":"Dora gives you the coins promised for protecting the apiary, but the bear is not going to give up the barrels. There's a skirmish ahead."},"E167.5":{"s":"You leave Dora with the pitchfork and the bear on the second barrel. Both see the party off with equally dissatisfied glances."},"E168.1":{"s":"The raven leads you to a hiding place under the roof of an old chapel, where hundreds of other people's trinkets ring. Among the finds is gold.","f":"Raven deliberately leads the party in circles until the evening; you don't find the real hiding place. The protracted chase consumes supplies."},"E168.2":{"s":"You allow the raven to continue his strange service. The toy crown lies at the King's feet for a while longer before the bird takes it back."},"E168.3":{"s":"The raven looks at the coins for a long time, then jumps on the hand and shows the place under the roof where other people's treasures are hidden. You find gold.","f":"The raven takes the offered coins and flies away without showing the way. He seems to have mastered the basics of trading very well."},"E168.4":{"s":"The raven ends up in your hands, but does not give away its hiding place even under the sternest royal gaze.","f":"The bird croaks shrilly, and dozens of its fellow birds fly off the roofs. It is no longer possible to hold the prey without a fight."},"E168.5":{"s":"The king takes the toy crown and hides it among the travel items. The raven bows importantly, as if he had been waiting for this particular reward for a long time."},"E169.1":{"s":"You change route, and the wolves silently accompany the caravan to a safe ford. Merchants pay in gold for staying alive."},"E169.2":{"s":"On the eastern road they find traces of an ambush and the belongings of the missing travelers; merchants reward your exploration with gold.","f":"As soon as the party enters the gorge, an armed enemy falls from the heights. The wolves warned not in vain: the battle begins."},"E169.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} walks along the edge of the wolf pack and notices traps hidden under fresh snow. Merchants give gold and supplies for the saved caravan.","f":"During reconnaissance, the danger that the wolves so persistently sensed bursts out of the snow. {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded while the others retreat.","v":{"nf":"The danger the wolves sensed bursts from beneath the snow, but none of the eligible fighters is gravely wounded. The scouts retreat."}},"E169.4":{"s":"The wolves retreat and the caravan passes the eastern road without delay. The merchants count out your gold payment.","f":"The flock rushes across the carts, not wanting to let them through to the eastern pass. A skirmish begins."},"E169.5":{"s":"You leave the merchants under the silent protection of wolves. They still don't take their eyes off the eastern road."},"E170.1":{"s":"Pat gets the gold, and the stallion, having ignored both noble riders, again chooses the Pawn. The horse breeder gloomily calls it “the new market.”"},"E170.2":{"s":"You decline the deal and leave the stallion's choice unresolved. He pointedly turns his back on Pat."},"E170.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} takes the stallion through a test: the horse trusts every movement and no longer makes attempts to throw off the rider.","f":"The stallion suddenly rears up; {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded. Pat stops the test and takes the animal to the stall.","v":{"nf":"The stallion rears up, but none of the available fighters is gravely wounded. Pat ends the trust test."}},"E170.4":{"s":"For the first time, Pat looks at the stallion not as a commodity, but as a future sire. For advice, he counts out gold to you.","f":"Pat assures that the horse must be sold, even if the horse himself does not agree with this. The conversation ends without a deal."},"E170.5":{"s":"The rich buyer pays for the right to be chosen, and the stallion again decides everything in his own way. You get gold, Pat gets a headache.","f":"The buyer requires guarantees of mutual sympathy, which no one can give. Pat removes the stallion from auction."},"E171.1":{"s":"You quietly turn your party around and retrace your steps. Not a single bird speaks until the forest is far behind."},"E171.2":{"s":"Beneath the dead deer you find an old pouch of coins that the restless shadow has not yet reached. You take the gold.","f":"The deer's shadow rises before you can touch its body. It is not alone, and a battle begins."},"E171.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} recognizes the boundary of someone else's spell without approaching the deer's body. The party finds a safe path and replenishes travel supplies.","f":"The shadow does not obey the usual laws of light; even {{heroName}} cannot understand what exactly lies under the deer."},"E171.4":{"s":"The flame pulls out someone else's shadow from under the deer, and it retreats into the thicket, leaving behind hidden gold.","f":"The shadow divides in two and rushes towards the fire from opposite sides. The party has to engage in a skirmish."},"E171.5":{"s":"You walk through the forest in silence, without looking at the birds, and at the edge of the forest you find supplies abandoned by previous travelers.","f":"Silence tightens around the party, and {{affectedHeroName}} falls, gravely wounded by an unknown force. The branches above the path never moved.","v":{"nf":"An unknown force forces the party to stop on a silent path, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The birds are silent."}},"E172.1":{"s":"You deliver a sealed package to a former fortress where cabbage is now sold. Khars cries with laughter and gives you a gold award."},"E172.2":{"s":"The sealed package holds an order long since made meaningless. Supplies survive beneath its old army wrapping; the tortoise shows no interest in the contents.","f":"Khars asks not to open the order, which his comrades did not have time to read. You leave the package sealed."},"E172.3":{"s":"You remove the travel rope from the turtle and release it without a new assignment. Khars salutes his former colleague."},"E172.4":{"s":"Khars gives away the old army shell for an agreed price. The turtle looks at him as if he had returned from the war for the first time in forty years."},"E172.5":{"s":"The party continues on their way, leaving the turtle to go to the fortress, which has been gone for a long time. Khars remains by the road with his unexpected past."},"E173.1":{"s":"Piri returns the shadow to the King's feet, weighing the coins in her palm. The shadow reluctantly takes its former place."},"E173.2":{"s":"The circle of light closes, and the fugitive shadow is forced to return to its owner. Piri gives the party supplies as a consolation.","f":"The shadow suddenly rushes out of the circle, and {{affectedHeroName}} falls under the blow of someone else's magic. Piri stops laughing.","v":{"nf":"The King's shadow escapes from the circle of light, but he is not gravely wounded. Piri stops laughing and hides her hands."}},"E173.3":{"s":"The shadow dances free for another hour and returns to the King's feet. Piri thanks you with travel supplies.","f":"The shadow uses the delay to climb where neither hands nor light can follow. The pursuit consumes supplies."},"E173.4":{"s":"Piri loses the duel and pays off with gold before returning the shadow to its place.","f":"Piri announces that the duel will not be verbal, but real. Instead of an argument about the shadow, a skirmish begins."},"E173.5":{"s":"The king takes a few steps without a shadow, and Piri is perplexed to see that her prank did not stop anyone.","f":"An escaped shadow confuses the tracks and leads the party off the path. We have to use up extra supplies."},"E174.1":{"s":"You remove the pear, and the ants walk around the sugar circle without being distracted by the sweets. The priestess gives you gold for a fair trial.","f":"The ants still head towards Tilly, and the priestess declares that the verdict has taken place. She has nothing to object to."},"E174.2":{"s":"You move the sweet bait closer, and the ants promptly change course. The priestess pays out gold without looking at the pear.","f":"The birds peck the pear before the ants have time to react. The trial continues in front of the confused priestess."},"E174.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} finds powdered sugar on the priestess’s fingers and understands who moved the bait. For exposure, the party receives gold and supplies.","f":"{{heroName}} finds nothing but sticky traces that the ants themselves managed to leave. Tilly continues to wait for the verdict."},"E174.4":{"s":"You declare the verdict invalid, and the ants calmly disperse to the pear. Tilly leaves the sugar circle.","f":"The priestess calls for the guards, declaring that the King has insulted an ancient custom. There's a skirmish ahead."},"E174.5":{"s":"You leave Tilly to wait for the ants' decision. Meanwhile, the priestess again carefully pushes the pear with her wand."},"E175.1":{"s":"The mask burns with an unpleasant giggle that ends only in ashes. Lum thanks you with gold.","f":"The flame goes out, and laughter begins to come from the faces of living people. A frightening confrontation becomes inevitable."},"E175.2":{"s":"The collector pays for the mask, which Lum refuses to even remove from the fabric. The party receives part of the gold.","f":"The buyer puts on the mask before paying, and its magic gravely wounds {{affectedHeroName}}. The bargain ends in a scream.","v":{"nf":"The mask laughs at the buyer's face and releases dangerous spells, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The deal falls through."}},"E175.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} unravels the laughter's binding spell, leaving the mask silent for the first time in years. Lum rewards you with gold and provisions.","f":"{{heroName}} opens one seal, but a second, even older one appears on the back. The actor asks not to unwrap the mask yet."},"E175.4":{"s":"You put on the mask for a moment and hear her laugh in your voice. After removing the spell, Lum pays in gold.","f":"Halfway to removing the mask, someone else's laughter breaks through your lips, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded from the outbreak of the spell.","v":{"nf":"Someone else's laughter breaks out from under the mask, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The mask is removed before the next flash."}},"E175.5":{"s":"You leave the mask wrapped and walk away. Already from a distance you can hear Lum persistently convincing the bundle to be silent."},"E176.1":{"s":"Nemi stops listening to the elders and whispers the child’s name herself. The flower opens again, and the family thanks you with supplies.","f":"Nemi almost decides to name the baby herself, but another elder announces a new sign on the petals. The dispute starts all over again."},"E176.2":{"s":"The fourth time, the flower reveals a pattern that all the elders finally read in the same way. Fairies thank you for your patience with gold.","f":"The flower opens with a completely new pattern; Nemi covers her face with her hands, and the anticipation eats up part of her travel supplies."},"E176.3":{"s":"The kid chooses a wooden spoon and happily knocks it on the ground. Nemi laughs and shares supplies with the party.","f":"The child grabs three objects at once and refuses to let go of even one. The elders announce that this is an even more complex sign."},"E176.4":{"s":"The elders agree to sell the unusual flower, and it is carefully transplanted into a road pot. Nemi can finally take care of the baby.","f":"The elders argue over the price and sacred status of the flower for so long that the deal falls through. All this time the baby calmly plays with a spoon."},"E176.5":{"s":"You leave Nemi to deal with the advice of the elders on her own. The blue flower opens again, but the child only looks at the spoon."},"E177.1":{"s":"Lala flies to a nearby rock with an indignant buzz, and the fairies begin repairs. They pay a gold reward for help.","f":"Lala spreads her wings and protects the bridge like her own fortress; {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded. Builders throw hammers.","v":{"nf":"Lala spreads her wings over the bridge, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. Builders are postponing repairs."}},"E177.2":{"s":"The builders are building the second bridge, but Lala remains under the familiar roof. The fairies share supplies for a peaceful exit."},"E177.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} calculates the new supports so that the old span remains Lala’s refuge. Builders pay in gold and add supplies.","f":"{{heroName}} offers a different drawing, but Lala does not even allow anyone to take measurements. The work is being postponed again."},"E177.4":{"s":"Lala inspects the proposed shelter, and then with an important look moves under the new canopy. The builders are finally approaching the old boards.","f":"Lala checks the new canopy and returns to the old bridge with a redoubled buzz. The fairies ask you not to say the word “moving” anymore."},"E177.5":{"s":"You ford the stream, leaving the fairies to argue with Lala over ownership. Behind you, the tiny hammers begin to ring once more."},"E178.1":{"s":"Butterfly leads the party out of the forest before anyone dares to ask for directions. Pat gives out supplies for passing the test.","f":"The butterfly disappears at the next turn, leaving the party among unfamiliar trees. In response to the call, only Pat's laughter is heard."},"E178.2":{"s":"Pat reluctantly admits that you are “between yesterday and the day after tomorrow,” and pays gold for your silence.","f":"The butterfly stops, folds its wings offendedly and refuses to lead further. Pat can't explain where the regular road is."},"E178.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} remembers every strange turn and leads the party back to the familiar sun. Pat thanks you in gold.","f":"{{heroName}} notices the trees repeating themselves, but the butterfly has already vanished into a passage beyond reach. {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded in the pursuit.","v":{"nf":"The butterfly disappears into an inaccessible passage, and when trying to catch up with it, none of the available fighters is gravely wounded. The shortcut is lost."}},"E178.4":{"s":"The butterfly lands on the outstretched hand, as if it had been waiting for an invitation for a long time, and stops leading the group in circles.","f":"The butterfly flaps its wings, and its disgruntled guardians emerge from the forest. A skirmish begins."},"E178.5":{"s":"You turn your party back to the usual road, although you have to walk all day to do this. The extra trek costs supplies."},"E179.1":{"s":"The King deftly parries the blow with his spoon and shatters Gubb's pot first. The chef solemnly concedes defeat and pays out the gold.","f":"Gubb unexpectedly turns out to be a master of the wooden spoon, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded. The assistants declare the chef's victory.","v":{"nf":"Gubb wins the duel with wooden spoons, but the King is not gravely wounded. The cook declares the test over."}},"E179.2":{"s":"Gubb accepts the apology in gold, pours the soup, and finally allows everyone to test its saltiness. The party gets supplies for the journey."},"E179.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} beats three blows with a giant spoon and is the first to split the agreed upon pot. Helpers pay in gold and share supplies.","f":"Gubb deftly knocks down his opponent's spoon; {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded. Assistants stop accepting bets.","v":{"nf":"Gubb knocks the spoon out of the champion's hand, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. Assistants stop accepting bets."}},"E179.4":{"s":"You find the real critic by description, and Gubb solemnly transfers his culinary grievances to him. You get gold for the investigation.","f":"No one remembers the critic except the cook, who suddenly begins to confuse the colors of the raincoats. The duel is still assigned to the King."},"E179.5":{"s":"You leave Gubb standing before his cauldron with a giant spoon. His final accusation follows you: “The soup won't insult itself!”"},"E180.1":{"s":"Shikk accepts the gold back that very day and reluctantly pays you the difference owed. Behind you, the accountants cross the first day off the contract.","f":"Shikk finds in the rules a fee for processing an early return. The treasury is losing gold, although the debt is formally closed."},"E180.2":{"s":"The deposit is returned with the accrued coins, and Shikk has no choice but to sign for the gain. Your treasury receives gold.","f":"On the back of the contract there is a small clause about a penalty for urgent withdrawal. The party loses some gold."},"E180.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} finds the point where the bank itself owes the client interest for the delay in payment. Shikk gives out gold, without ceasing to click his abacus.","f":"Shikk deftly shifts the counting tokens and demonstrates that, under the bank's rules, the bank is always right. {{heroName}} gives up the argument."},"E180.4":{"s":"You cut the debtor's rope and remove him from the custody of the accountants. A new companion joins the party.","f":"Two armed accountants shield the cart, declaring the attempted release a “violation of credit discipline.” A skirmish begins.","v":{"rs":"The debtor is released from the accountants, but there is no room for him in your party. He leaves gold in gratitude for his freedom."}},"E180.5":{"s":"You pass by a bank on wheels. The man with the sign about the fourth day looks after you with special understanding."},"E181.1":{"s":"You uphold Plyukha's technical victory, and Tick immediately claims the prize money. He shares some of the gold with your party."},"E181.2":{"s":"The finishing tape is returned to its place, the rats go out onto the track, and Plyukha wins with his own paws. The organizers pay gold.","f":"Tick declares the re-race a violation of the original rules, and the outraged jockeys grab their guns. Instead of a race, a skirmish begins."},"E181.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} finds a compulsory rule: to win, a racer must cross the line after the start. Tick pays up and angrily wakes Plyukha.","f":"{{heroName}} reads the charter to the end, but Tick's loophole turns out to be legal. Plyukha continues to snore at the finish line."},"E181.4":{"s":"Plyukha wakes at precisely the right moment and overtakes the others at the final bend. Your wager wins gold.","f":"Plyukha sleeps through the starting signal, and the bookmakers keep your stake. Tick calmly calls it training."},"E181.5":{"s":"You are not involved in the sleeping winner debate. Behind you you can hear the jockeys calling louder and louder for the missing judge."},"E182.1":{"s":"You follow the map to a cave and uncover treasure worthy even of a golden map. Its coins swell your treasury.","f":"Nib kept silent about the fact that the cave was guarded by armed inhabitants. Instead of an easy trip for the treasure, a skirmish begins."},"E182.2":{"s":"You send the gold map to the smelter, not caring about the route on the back. The proceeds return to the treasury."},"E182.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} checks the cave before Nib and finds a cache that the merchant wanted to sell twice. For the discovery, the party receives gold.","f":"The cave turns out to be a trap; {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded, and the golden tablet remains with Nib.","v":{"nf":"The cave turns out to be a trap, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The golden tablet remains with Nib."}},"E182.4":{"s":"Nib is forced to admit that he is primarily selling the gold plate, and not the direction to the treasure. As a result of the bargaining, the party gets gold.","f":"The goblin declares the map a work of art and raises his price, claiming you've insulted its maker. The talks go nowhere."},"E182.5":{"s":"You decline to buy a map engraved on what is itself a treasure. Nib shouts after you: “That's premium quality!”"},"E183.1":{"s":"The boards fly apart, and pickled mushrooms are actually found inside, which the party takes on the road. The beetle hears silence for the first time.","f":"The barrel responds to the blow with a tirade of such force that it splits the adjacent container. The party loses some of its supplies."},"E183.2":{"s":"Beetle happily pockets the coins and parts with the most talkative cargo of his career. At farewell, the barrel offers an opinion of its own."},"E183.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} deciphers the runes in the wood, finally silencing the enchanted barrel. Beetle rewards you with gold and supplies.","f":"The barrel argues with each rune removed, and then begins to swear in another language. {{heroName}} prefers to postpone work."},"E183.4":{"s":"A nearby magician recognizes his colleague's old work and immediately buys the barrel. The proceeds replenish the treasury.","f":"The magician refuses to take the barrel back after hearing the first phrase from under the lid. The beetle remains with its cargo."},"E183.5":{"s":"You leave Beetle arguing with the enchanted barrel. Around the corner, its indignant voice rings out: “And you call this transport?”"},"E184.1":{"s":"Brick rises from the coffin, hearing that the insurance agent is already checking his breathing with a mirror. Tana gives out gold for the stopped performance.","f":"Brick lies motionless even after hot soup is brought under his nose. The agent states that there is still insufficient evidence of life activity."},"E184.2":{"s":"Brick remains in the coffin until the ceremony is over, and the insurance agent reluctantly issues the payout. The party receives part of the gold.","f":"Brick sneezes too loudly, and the agent demands to return the amount already received with a fine. The party loses gold."},"E184.3":{"s":"The agent checks Brick's pulse, discovers a suspiciously healthy heartbeat for a corpse, and closes the claim. You receive gold for your legal ingenuity.","f":"The agent assures that a heartbeat is not included in the list of life signs. Brick carefully opens one eye to hear the continuation."},"E184.4":{"s":"Brick crawls out of the coffin and admits that it is high time for him to change his profession. A new companion joins your party.","f":"Brick considers the hike too dangerous and returns under the coffin lid. Tana asks you not to disturb the “dead man” anymore.","v":{"rs":"Brick is ready to change professions and join the party, but there is no room for him. He gives you gold in thanks for a new chance at life."}},"E184.5":{"s":"You leave the funeral to continue as scheduled. The insurance agent sighs again as Brick sneezes."},"E185.1":{"s":"Emma stops the bleeding, and for the first time the patient stops asking about the third doctor. The caravan leaders thank you with gold.","f":"While Emma is preparing bandages, the wounded man's condition worsens; Precious supplies go towards additional aid."},"E185.2":{"s":"Crick quickly treats the wound, and the patient seems surprised to discover he is still alive. The goblin receives his fee and gives your party a share.","f":"Crick rushes the operation and catches {{affectedHeroName}} with a sharp instrument. The new wound needs treatment of its own.","v":{"nf":"Crick catches the patient with an instrument, but none of the eligible fighters is gravely wounded. The examination must be stopped."}},"E185.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} forces Emma and Crick to divide the work into stages; together they save the caravan driver. For order, the party gets gold and supplies.","f":"Even {{heroName}} cannot stop the dispute about the sequence of procedures. The doctors continue to bicker on the stretcher."},"E185.4":{"s":"You lay out the necessary travel supplies in front of the doctors, and they finally stop arguing about the instruments. The patient thanks you barely audibly."},"E185.5":{"s":"You leave Emma and Crick to argue over whose turn it is to help. The patient quietly asks whether anyone has found the third doctor.","f":"You leave before the doctors reach an agreement, and a new argument follows. The caravan driver remains waiting for help."},"E186.1":{"s":"The goblins take the baby and the she-wolf is killed at the roots of the tree, even though she was protecting the child. The family pays gold for his return."},"E186.2":{"s":"You stop the goblins and show how the she-wolf covered the child with her tail. The parents take the baby, leave you supplies and let the beast leave.","f":"The goblins mistake the she-wolf's protection for a threat to their child and rush at the party with torches. A skirmish begins."},"E186.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} sits down at the roots and waits patiently for the she-wolf to let the baby go. The grateful family gives the party gold.","f":"The she-wolf is frightened by the movement, rushes to protect the child, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The she-wolf drives back the approaching rescuers, but none of the eligible fighters is gravely wounded. The child remains beneath the roots."}},"E186.4":{"s":"You give the goblins some of the food for the she-wolf and ask them not to pursue her. The parents agree as the child reaches for the familiar ear again."},"E186.5":{"s":"You do not intervene when parents approach the baby cautiously. The she-wolf watches them from under the roots and does not let the baby out of sight."},"E187.1":{"s":"The angelic ritual separates the intruding voices without taking Neven's own. Sael leaves gold in thanks for your help.","f":"During the cleansing, an alien force strikes in a circle and gravely wounds {{affectedHeroName}}. Neven is left with three votes.","v":{"nf":"The cleansing circle is disrupted, but none of the eligible combatants are gravely wounded. Two alien voices remain in Neven."}},"E187.2":{"s":"Mor pronounces the words of the ritual, and Neven again responds only with his voice. The demon leaves the party gold for their support.","f":"The Rite of Mora opens a rift from which armed creatures emerge. The battle begins."},"E187.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} first listens to Neven and builds the ritual around his consent, rather than the demands of the spirits. The ritual frees him and the party receives the gold.","f":"{{heroName}} finds a safe start to the ritual, but the necessary components are missing. An unfinished attempt consumes supplies."},"E187.4":{"s":"You leave Sael, Mor and Neven to find a solution between the three of them. The last voice heard is Neven himself, demanding the right to have the first word."},"E187.5":{"s":"You forcefully sever the ties between Neven and both spirits. The freed man gives the party the gold, while the angel and demon are already arguing outside.","f":"The two spirits resist being banished and call upon their armed defenders. The battle begins."},"E188.1":{"s":"You use up some of your supplies by helping Borda secure the stone span around the trunk. The dwarf pays in gold for completed work."},"E188.2":{"s":"You bring Liel the necessary materials, and the roots stop putting pressure on the future foundation. The elf supplies the party with supplies in gratitude."},"E188.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} combines Borda's calculations with Liel's living supports. The bridge curves around the tree without harming it, and both craftsmen reward you with gold and supplies.","f":"{{heroName}} discovers that some of the supports are on living roots, and cannot complete the project without a new calculation. Work is postponed."},"E188.4":{"s":"After a bitter dispute, Borda receives permission to remove the tree, and the contractor pays gold to speed up construction. Liel leaves silently.","f":"Liel refuses to let the axes get close to the trunk and calls for the defenders of the forest. A skirmish begins."},"E188.5":{"s":"You do not interfere with the work of the masters. Borda checks the corners again, and Liel removes another root from the masonry."},"E189.1":{"s":"You explain to Grom that the lake in the poem is not an ambush. The baffled orc rewards the lesson with supplies.","f":"Grom insists that the calm water is a front line and recites the ballad like orders for an attack. He refuses to accept Elian's meaning."},"E189.2":{"s":"Elian agrees that a strange version of Grom also has the right to sound around the fire. In gratitude, she gives gold for helping in reconciliation.","f":"Elian is not ready to call a song about her beloved lake a military march. Grom continues to pound his fist on his knee."},"E189.3":{"s":"Elian writes the words, and Grom finds a rhythm that finally suits both. A new battle song brings supplies to the party from grateful listeners.","f":"They cannot even agree on the first verse: the elf demands silence, and the orc demands a drum. There is no joint song."},"E189.4":{"s":"Copies of the thunderous version of the ballad are readily taken apart in the orc camp. The proceeds replenish the treasury.","f":"Buyers demand their money back: the song promised a battle, and none took place. They take their gold from you while Elian watches with a weary smile."},"E189.5":{"s":"You sit by the fire and listen to Grom roar a ballad about a quiet lake. Elian shuts her eyes at the particularly thunderous word “tenderness.”"},"E190.1":{"s":"The king accepts Yoss's arguments and pays him the due amount from the treasury. The skeleton carefully signs the sheet and asks to call the next one."},"E190.2":{"s":"The Treasurer decides to stop payments on death and issues gold to settle the case. Yoss folds his ID and promises to file a complaint."},"E190.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} creates a separate category for returning veterans without rewriting the old records. The treasury pays your party gold for settling the dispute.","f":"{{heroName}} proposes a new order, but officials are arguing about what date to count the return to service. The list remains open."},"E190.4":{"s":"Yoss decides that the new service is better than an endless queue for the treasury, and joins the party with the same certificate.","f":"Yoss refuses to trade his well-deserved pension for another military campaign. He remains at the window with the folder.","v":{"rs":"Yoss is ready to enlist, but he cannot accept a new fighter. The treasurer gives the party gold instead of concluding a contract."}},"E190.5":{"s":"You pass Yoss's folder to the next official. The skeleton calmly takes a turn at another window."},"E191.1":{"s":"You recognize Hark's right to the fire-breathing mechanism, and he pays gold for confirmation of the patent. Slip puts out his hat."},"E191.2":{"s":"You approve Slip's patent, and the goblin immediately counts out the reward in gold. Hark leaves, loudly discussing the safety of the tests.","f":"Slip tries to repeat the demonstration, the explosion spoils the supplies, and they have to be written off. The patent decision is postponed."},"E191.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} proves that Hark's breath and Slip's pickled peppers are different sources of flame. Both inventors pay for the examination in gold and supplies.","f":"{{heroName}} finds a general diagram, but cannot establish the authorship of the early drawing. The patent litigation continues."},"E191.4":{"s":"You give Slip the gold for the prototype and receive a device tied with straps. The Goblin advises not to place it next to hats.","f":"You pay for the prototype, but Slip cannot bring it into working condition. Spent coins are not returned."},"E191.5":{"s":"You ban both devices until safe testing, and the disputants pay gold for their decision. Slip hides his charred hat.","f":"Hark challenges the ban, and Slip is already preparing his next explosive experiment. The decision cannot be implemented."},"E192.1":{"s":"You leave food near the stairs, and the spider carefully climbs down to take the bait. Iara and Tal escape the roof and reward you with gold.","f":"The spider rushes for the bait straight to the fighters, mistaking them for a threat. A skirmish begins."},"E192.2":{"s":"Iara gives the familiar command, and the spider frees the stairs. For their help, she gives the party gold.","f":"The spider resists the command and knocks one of the rescuers off the roof: {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The spider pushes the rescuers away from the stairs, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The trio remains on the roof."}},"E192.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} feigns the rescuers' departure, drawing the spider to the far edge of the roof. Iara and Tal climb down and pay you in gold.","f":"The spider does not respond to the trick {{heroName}} and continues to block the stairs. Rescue fails."},"E192.4":{"s":"You dismantle a safe section of the destroyed roof and make a new descent. Both rescued people give the gold to the party.","f":"The slabs crumble before the exit is ready; Supplies are used to strengthen the supports. Iara and Tal remain upstairs for now."},"E192.5":{"s":"You don't get involved in an argument on the roof. The spider sits between Iara and Tal, like a guard dog with eight legs."},"E193.1":{"s":"You persuade Mim to leave B-12 and find another hiding place. Ord rewards the return of his automaton with gold.","f":"The mime calls upon the workshop fairies for help when you try to remove it from its body. A skirmish begins."},"E193.2":{"s":"You acknowledge the agreement between Mim and B-12, and the machine joyfully plays its first tune. Ord is reluctant to share his supplies with you."},"E193.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} installs the second remote control, and Mim and B-12 distribute control without dispute. Ord thanks with gold and supplies for a working solution.","f":"{{heroName}} detects that the accounting module is already occupied by the fairy, and there are no free connectors. The rework has to be postponed."},"E193.4":{"s":"You pay for the upgraded B-12, and the automaton with Mim inside joins your party. Delighted laughter rises from its vents.","f":"Ord refuses to sell the machine until the inspection is completed, although the advance has already been made. The party is left without a new fighter.","v":{"rs":"Ord agrees to sell B-12, but your party has no room for another fighter. He keeps the automaton in his workshop and compensates you in gold."}},"E193.5":{"s":"You leave Ord to argue with Mim and B-12. The automaton wants to play music; the fairy insists on cancelling the modification."},"E194.1":{"s":"You buy back an object one of your fighters recognises and return it to its owner. The hero holds it silently in both hands."},"E194.2":{"s":"You give the merchants an unnecessary relic, from which no one in the party expects any use anymore. The market pays in gold.","f":"The merchant notices that you still hope to return the relic and refuses the deal. There is no sale."},"E194.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} questions the traders and finds out how the item got on the counter. In gratitude, they donate travel supplies to the party.","f":"{{heroName}} receives only evasive answers: in this market the origin of things is not discussed. Nothing useful can be learned."},"E194.4":{"s":"You find an item among forgotten little things that a collector is willing to pay for in real gold. The proceeds replenish the treasury.","f":"The merchant demands a fee for taking a long time to examine the items you refused to buy. The party loses gold."},"E194.5":{"s":"You leave the night market without acknowledging that you have stopped looking for anything lost. The familiar object remains on the table."},"E195.1":{"s":"You address the bridge as if it were an old friend, and the stone railings move aside. The grateful caravan shares its supplies.","f":"The bridge responds with the usual “wrong” even to a polite request. The crossing remains closed."},"E195.2":{"s":"After searching through the old names, the bridge recognizes the forgotten message of the builder and opens the way. The caravan thanks with gold.","f":"You search through names and dates until nightfall. The bridge repeats its refusal, and the long wait uses up supplies."},"E195.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} restores the words “say as a friend” on the arch, and travelers find the correct address to the bridge. The caravan pays in gold and supplies.","f":"{{heroName}} detects only half of the phrase and cannot restore the lost characters. The bridge remains locked."},"E195.4":{"s":"You spend some of your supplies going around the ford and come out to the other side. The stone bridge once again demands a password."},"E195.5":{"s":"You knock out some stones and open a passage through the damaged span. The bridge falls silent, although its railings visibly sag.","f":"A blow to the masonry awakens the bridge's defenders, and armed guards emerge from both banks. The battle begins."},"E196.1":{"s":"You remember the warning without demanding an explanation from the old man. In parting, he points out a cache of supplies, which the King, according to him, had already found once."},"E196.2":{"s":"The old man without hesitation reveals the King's childhood secret and shows the place where the food for the road is hidden. The party takes supplies.","f":"The old man answers the question too generally, and the evidence does not convince the King. At a fork in the road you will have to decide for yourself."},"E196.3":{"s":"You hold a stranger at a fire until dawn and find an old coined purse in his possession. Gold enters the treasury.","f":"As you try to hold the stranger, he seizes the King's sleeve. {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded; by morning the old man is gone.","v":{"nf":"An attempt to restrain the old man turns into a dangerous collision, but the King is not gravely wounded. The stranger disappears before dawn."}},"E196.4":{"s":"The old man looks at one of his companions and only answers: “He himself must choose what to remember.” No one gets any proof or predictions.","f":"The old man refuses to reveal someone else's future and puts out the fire with the last coal. There will be no answer to the question."},"E196.5":{"s":"You refuse to believe the man in the worn crown. He doesn’t argue, he just looks again at where the left fork will be tomorrow."},"E197.1":{"s":"You pay for the night and for the first time see how an orc yields to an angel in cards without a single insult. In the morning, the innkeeper gives out supplies, but outside the gate there is no longer a tavern itself."},"E197.2":{"s":"At the shared table no one cheats, and a lucky hand wins gold for your party. Even the goblin congratulates the winner sincerely.","f":"The cards turn against you, and the silent elf by the window collects your stake. By morning, the tavern has vanished—along with any hope of a rematch."},"E197.3":{"s":"For the first time, guests talk about roads, without trying to hide dangerous places from former enemies. The innkeeper packs supplies for the journey for an attentive conversation.","f":"Each guest remembers a different road, and their stories contradict each other. The party does not receive reliable instructions."},"E197.4":{"s":"You carry the sword inside, despite the weight of the hilt, and the guests give you the golden purse they won in a dispute. The innkeeper silently returns the blade to the door.","f":"The weapon slips from the hands and damages the camp bag at the threshold. Some supplies have to be thrown away."},"E197.5":{"s":"You pass by bright windows and do not check the rules of the night world. At dawn, only an empty roadside remains behind."},"E198.1":{"s":"You take turns watching until dawn, spending supplies through the night. Vena pays in gold when the statue remains twelve paces from her tent."},"E198.2":{"s":"Everyone looks away at once, and the statue appears beside the tent without touching anyone. Vena finds goldwork inside its pedestal.","f":"The statue reaches the tent and turns around to face the party. Armed guards rise from the stone and the battle begins."},"E198.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} erects a blank box without slits for observation around the statue. Vena pays in gold for a successful way to stop its movement.","f":"{{heroName}} notices that the statue moves when the last hole is closed. It cannot be locked safely."},"E198.4":{"s":"You break a stone figure while several people are watching it at once. Gold is discovered inside the debris.","f":"From the first blow, the statue splits, and the revived defenders of the excavation emerge from it. A skirmish begins."},"E198.5":{"s":"You withdraw the party from the excavation site, leaving Vena to observe it. At parting, the statue stands already eleven steps from the tent."},"E199.1":{"s":"The King speaks plainly about why he travels, and the last glass on the table fills of its own accord. The strangers unblock the door, leaving gold and supplies.","f":"The hall demands a confession the King refuses to make. The stone chair gravely wounds him, and the dinner does not end.","v":{"nf":"The thirteenth chair tightens around the King, but no serious injury occurs. The door remains closed."}},"E199.2":{"s":"The King names his invented purpose so confidently that the writing fades from the wall. A prize in gold for the convincing lie remains on the table.","f":"The thirteenth card flashes, exposing the lie, and one by one the guests raise their weapons. The battle begins."},"E199.3":{"s":"You find out that each guest did not come of their own free will, but for an answer to someone else’s question. The inscription disappears, and the grateful prisoners leave the gold.","f":"The guests argue about the words “why” and “came”, but do not find a common answer. The hall does not let anyone go."},"E199.4":{"s":"You find a hidden doorway mechanism and lead the party out without participating in dinner. They remain at the table to wait for the thirteenth guest.","f":"Trying to break the wall causes strangers to form a circle around the exit. A skirmish begins."},"E199.5":{"s":"One of the companions sits in the royal seat and is responsible for himself, not for the King. The hall opens a passage, leaving supplies for the party.","f":"The card continues to show the King's name, no matter who you replace him with at the table. The exit does not appear."},"E200.1":{"s":"The master accepts the payment, lays the slab “towards the city” and taps the seams with a hammer. On the new road, you find supplies at a roadside warehouse."},"E200.2":{"s":"You choose a slab with the strangest direction, and the road leads straight to a forgotten gold cache.","f":"The path leads you in circles around its own intentions. You waste supplies searching for the exit while the mason watches with professional sympathy."},"E200.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} notices solid ground beyond the border of the path and makes a passage without a master. Along the way, gold and supplies are discovered.","f":"The new path collapses under the scout's feet, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The unfortified ground is torn away during reconnaissance, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The road cannot be paved."}},"E200.4":{"s":"The old man names the master who once laid the first stones of the old tract, and shows the payment niche in the last pillar. There is gold there.","f":"The master replies that there were too many builders to remember the first one. The party does not receive gold for telling a story."},"E200.5":{"s":"You step off the last slab and walk straight along untouched grass. The master follows the group with his gaze, as if someone had just built a road without stones."},"E201.1":{"s":"Lott takes eight coins and issues a receipt for your right to use the city's shadow. Clerk Vena stamps it without looking up."},"E201.2":{"s":"You force Lott to count the illegally taken fees and return them to the queue. The remaining gold according to the calculation goes to the treasury.","f":"The collector calls the city guards, declaring the demand for return a rebellion against the treasury. A skirmish begins."},"E201.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} finds in the resolution a clause about payment for voluntary service, but no one ordered the shadow. Lott returns the gold and the line bursts into laughter.","f":"{{heroName}} discovers an application with an exception for the city wall, and officials are collecting legal costs. The party loses gold."},"E201.4":{"s":"You lead the party under the scorching sun past the booth, without ever stepping into the city shadow. Lott doesn't know how to formalize such a violation of the tariff spirit."},"E202.1":{"s":"You persuade Khas to let every farmer use the mill for the same price. The grateful farmers send provisions for your journey.","f":"The miller locks the gate and delays the line with grain. You have to spend your own supplies while waiting."},"E202.2":{"s":"You pay the price of Khas and receive three bundles of flour and crackers. There is still not a single leaf moving in the valley."},"E202.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} finds a hidden air channel under the foundation and opens its damper. Farmers pay in gold and provide supplies for the returned wind.","f":"The fastening of the millstone in the tower breaks off, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded. The mystery of the wind remains unsolved.","v":{"nf":"A damaged mechanism stops the check, but no eligible combatants are gravely wounded. The mill continues to hold the wind."}},"E202.4":{"s":"You drive around a mill, whose circle rotates in complete calm. Behind him, the boy is again trying to lift the kite."},"E203.1":{"s":"You manage to restrain the faceless customer, and Ren finds a purse of gold in his clothes. The stranger himself never says a word.","f":"The faceless man slips free and summons armed servants from the back room. A skirmish begins."},"E203.2":{"s":"You throw the portrait into the fire, and the unpleasant resemblance disappears along with the paint. The faceless stranger leaves the inn without looking back.","f":"When the canvas catches fire, someone else's hand comes out of the flames, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The portrait bursts into dangerous flame, but none of the eligible combatants are gravely wounded. The party does not recognize the customer's intentions."}},"E203.3":{"s":"You give Ren the gold and fold up the unfinished portrait. The artist assures that he will no longer paint people according to the instructions of the faceless."},"E203.4":{"s":"You leave the inn before the stranger can speak. Ren is left with a brush in his hand and the King's face on the canvas."},"E204.1":{"s":"Under oath, the brothers finally name who got the bridge, the treasury and the arrest. The village gives out gold for the restoration of order.","f":"The seven say the same oaths in the same voices. Sela closes the list: the roll call did not decide anything."},"E204.2":{"s":"You pay six gold pieces for clearing the passage and leave the outpost. All seven sergeants salute at the same time."},"E204.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} identifies one brother by the way he holds his spear and another by his stride. The village pays gold for finally making sense of the brothers' assignments.","f":"{{heroName}} notices that the brothers managed to exchange drill habits. The culprit cannot be determined."},"E204.4":{"s":"One of the seven Brants agrees to join your party, where it will at least be easier to distinguish himself from his colleagues.","f":"The brothers cannot agree on who exactly is signing up, and all seven remain at the outpost.","v":{"rs":"One of the seven Brants agrees to serve, but your party has no room for another fighter. Sela rewards your attempt to relieve the outpost with gold."}},"E205.1":{"s":"You open the locked town hall and find Coven still sitting over a three-day-old meal. The townspeople pay you gold for ending his endless meeting with a spoon.","f":"At the sound of a break-in, armed guards from the mayor's quarters emerge from the town hall. A skirmish begins."},"E205.2":{"s":"You hand over the gold to the guards, and the city gates finally open. Secretary Lida asks not to ask questions about dessert."},"E205.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} discovers that the voice comes from an enchanted spoon, not Coven. Lida rewards the discovery with supplies.","f":"{{heroName}} trespasses the enchanted room, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"An attempt to check the voices is thwarted by magical protection, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The mayor remains at the table."}},"E205.4":{"s":"You use up your supplies to bypass the closed gate and exit to the next road. From the window of the town hall comes the constant: “I’m not finished yet!”"},"E206.1":{"s":"You walk over the hill with Pierce and help him try on the boot while Ani checks the seams. The giant stamps his foot contentedly and pays the shoemaker gold, part of which he shares.","f":"When trying it on, the side seam comes apart, and you have to repair the boot right on the giant’s foot. The party's supplies go to work."},"E206.2":{"s":"You give Pierce the gold and take travel supplies from the workshop. Ani warns not to place bags near the giant's sole."},"E206.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} keeps the giant talking about long roads while Pierce adjusts his tight sock. For a saved fitting, the shoemaker gives out gold.","f":"The giant suddenly steps his foot, forgetting about the little guests, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The giant steps awkwardly, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The fitting ends without a reward."}},"E206.4":{"s":"You leave Pierce and Ani to wrestle with the enormous boot. From beyond the hill comes a booming “READY?”"},"E207.1":{"s":"At night a traveller in wet boots appears beneath the spring-green maple, but Saire does not recognise his face. The stranger leaves provisions and disappears before dawn.","f":"Instead of Saire's brother, armed strangers follow the wet footprints out of the forest. A skirmish begins."},"E207.2":{"s":"You convince Saire not to wait beneath the tree alone for another night. She rewards you with gold and leaves without looking back.","f":"Saire points to fresh tracks and refuses to leave where her brother might return. You cannot persuade her."},"E207.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} traces the wet prints to the roots and finds an old bookmark with gold there. The maple continues to turn green in autumn.","f":"The roots respond to {{heroName}}'s touch with a sudden jerk, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The roots push the explorers out of the clearing, but none of the eligible combatants are gravely wounded. The trail remains unexplained."}},"E207.4":{"s":"You leave Sayre under the spring crown among the fallen autumn leaves. There is only one chain of wet footprints left on the trail."},"E208.1":{"s":"The party passes through the garden without saying a word, and on their way out they find a stockpile of supplies at the gatehouse. The trees never repeat the royal voice.","f":"In the silence, ancient orders come to life, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded from the activated garden defense.","v":{"nf":"The old garden defense works, but no eligible combatants are gravely wounded. The passage ends without a find."}},"E208.2":{"s":"You answer an order you have not yet spoken. The garden offers a golden bookmark from a hollow, and Erel dares not ask who began the conversation.","f":"The trees take the answer to a military order and release the ancient guard. A skirmish begins."},"E208.3":{"s":"You pay Erel for a detour and pass behind the garden without disturbing his memory. On distant branches, someone continues to repeat other people's orders."},"E208.4":{"s":"You leave the garden, where the trees remember words not yet spoken. Around the bend, the royal voice finally fades away."},"E209.1":{"s":"You wait for the bees to return to one of the elves on their own. Liel thanks you for your patience with supplies.","f":"The swarm does not leave the Queen even in the evening, and supplies are spent waiting. The ceremony remains unfinished."},"E209.2":{"s":"One of the candidates carefully approaches the Queen, and golden bees fly over to her. Liel pays gold for finding a way out.","f":"The bees do not accept the proposed replacement, and the candidate retreats from the buzzing cloud. The choice remains the same."},"E209.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} completes the ritual so that the swarm conveys the sign to the chosen elf. Liel hands the party gold and supplies.","f":"{{heroName}} tries to transmit the sign, but the bees return to their previous choice. The elves refuse to accept the new outcome."},"E209.4":{"s":"The bees follow the party to the road and leave the collected supplies at the campsite. Only after this the swarm returns to the garden.","f":"The swarm refuses to leave its chosen Queen, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded during the withdrawal.","v":{"nf":"The swarm stops the withdrawal, but none of the eligible combatants are gravely wounded. It is not possible to take the bees with you."}},"E210.1":{"s":"You pay with part of the supplies for the boat crossing downstream. Tevir does not look up at the site of the missing bridge."},"E210.2":{"s":"An invisible stone flooring is discovered underfoot, and in the middle of the river the party finds old gold.","f":"The invisible span gives way, gravely wounding {{affectedHeroName}} in the fall into the river.","v":{"nf":"Invisible support disappears underfoot, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The party returns to the shore without any prey."}},"E210.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} finds places of old supports along the water flow and leads the party to hidden reserves on the other bank. Your supplies are replenished.","f":"The erroneous support goes away from under his feet, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The line of invisible supports turns out to be unreliable, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The transition is postponed."}},"E210.4":{"s":"You leave the river to flow around a bridge that no longer exists. In the darkening water, someone again steps on the invisible stone."},"E211.1":{"s":"You wait at the only footprint until an invisible creature reveals itself by moving the grass. The party finds gold in the lair he left behind.","f":"An invisible beast bypasses the ambush and rushes at the deployed fighters. A skirmish begins."},"E211.2":{"s":"You leave some of the provisions at the imprint and leave. The grass bends around the gift, not around your feet."},"E211.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} guesses the movement of the beast through the grass and finds its cache of gold and supplies.","f":"A sudden blow from an invisible paw gravely wounds {{affectedHeroName}}. The pursuit stops.","v":{"nf":"The invisible beast slips free, but none of the eligible fighters is gravely wounded. The hunt yields nothing."}},"E211.4":{"s":"You walk around a single imprint along a rocky slope. Behind you, the grass bends again - this time without you."},"E212.1":{"s":"You leave Arena to search for the last note without outside advice. The student carefully adjusts his cloak while the empty hall waits to continue."},"E212.2":{"s":"You choose a simple ending for the melody, and the stone hall answers with one clear chord. Aren rewards you with gold for finally bringing the piece to a close.","f":"A wrong note causes the stone seats to move and armed guards emerge from underneath them. A skirmish begins."},"E212.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} helps Aren hear what the melody was going for, rather than guessing its ending. The hall opens a cache of gold and supplies.","f":"{{heroName}} finds only a repeating motif, but not the answer to it. The teacher continues to rehearse the unfinished song."},"E212.4":{"s":"You leave supplies for the musicians and ask the student to make sure that Aren at least eats. Under the stone arches the penultimate note sounds again."},"E213.1":{"s":"You give Urgu a symbolic tribute, and he is relieved to thank you for the “civilized cooperation.” The orcs release the party along the road without a fight."},"E213.2":{"s":"You praise the leader for his politeness and offer to receive payment for guarding the road instead of robbery. Urg gives out supplies for a successful idea.","f":"One of the orcs tears down the complaint sign and demands a real raid. Urg does not have time to stop the skirmish."},"E213.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} learns that the rank-and-file orcs would gladly guard travellers for pay, if only it spared them memorising speeches. Urg rewards the new arrangement with gold.","f":"Ordinary orcs fear their superiors more than they hate paper threats. {{heroName}} returns without agreement."},"E213.4":{"s":"You abandon polite procedure and accept the challenge according to the old custom. Urg folds the piece of paper: a skirmish begins."},"E214.1":{"s":"You give Grum supplies, and the cook corrects the seasoning of the huge cauldron. Chieftain Sharg pays gold without asking for another taste."},"E214.2":{"s":"Sharg tastes the soup again and finally declares it passable. Grum rewards you with gold for saving his job.","f":"The leader takes a sip and demands to punish the one who advised him to do this. A skirmish begins."},"E214.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} calculates the cauldron's capacity and adjusts the proportions before the elders. Grum gives you gold and provisions.","f":"{{heroName}} discovers that the cook has added salt twice, but there is no water supply to correct it. Lunch has to be postponed."},"E214.4":{"s":"You leave the orc camp to decide the size of a single pinch. Grum stares at the cauldron as though it might answer for itself."},"E215.1":{"s":"You award the stool to Drag, and the clan pays gold for the recognized right to the relic. Mog crosses his arms in displeasure.","f":"Mog rejects the decision and leads his warriors to their rivals. A skirmish begins."},"E215.2":{"s":"You acknowledge Mog's right to the stool, and his family thanks the party with supplies. Drag looks at the only surviving leg for a long time.","f":"Drag considers the decision an insult to the memory of his grandfather and challenges his supporters to a confrontation."},"E215.3":{"s":"You pay both clans the price of the disputed stool and take it from the field. The leaders are left quarreling without a reason, although they are trying to find a new one."},"E215.4":{"s":"You propose to decide the right to the stool by duel, and the leaders joyfully take up arms. A skirmish begins."},"E215.5":{"s":"You do not undertake to share a dilapidated stool between two clans. There is a cracking sound of wood behind you, as if the story is ending itself."},"E216.1":{"s":"You tell Tara and Brock that the ability to spot danger before the fight also serves the clan. Kurg thanks you for the opportunity to be heard and gives you supplies.","f":"Brock considers support a sign of weakness and assigns Kurg a new test. The conversation does not change the family's decision."},"E216.2":{"s":"Kurg undergoes a short reconnaissance test and for the first time does not see blood. He happily enrolls in the party.","f":"Kurg does not dare to go out for the test without a senior instructor and remains in the camp. The party does not receive a new companion.","v":{"rs":"Kurg passes the scouting test, but there is no room for him in your ranks. Tara gives you gold for helping him prove himself."}},"E216.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} tests Kurg for stealth and observation, and the young orc shows real talent. He joins the party.","f":"Kurg confuses the signals during the check, but helps to collect provisions after a failure. The party receives supplies, but without a new scout.","v":{"rs":"{{heroName}} confirms Kurg's talent, but your party has no room for a scout. The orcs reward you with gold and keep him among them."}},"E216.4":{"s":"You do not interfere in the decision of the first test of Kurg. Brock takes out the knife again, and Tara is already preparing to catch her son."},"E217.1":{"s":"You leave supplies in front of the disgruntled boulder as an apology. The stone face slowly turns away from the road."},"E217.2":{"s":"You pull away the boulder, and the hunters thank you with gold for freeing the passage. The stone grumbles, but remains by the path.","f":"The boulder suddenly rolls and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The stone rolls back onto the path, but none of the eligible combatants are gravely wounded. The passage remains closed."}},"E217.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} pronounces the prescribed words of reconciliation, and the face on the stone smoothes out. Grateful hunters supply the party with supplies.","f":"The boulder rejects the ritual and rolls onto {{affectedHeroName}}'s leg, inflicting a grave wound.","v":{"nf":"The stone rejects the ritual, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The face on the boulder remains unhappy."}},"E217.4":{"s":"You spend some of your supplies on a long walk around the sacred boulder. The hunters continue to apologize with a straight face."},"E218.1":{"s":"You remain behind the palisade until dawn, spending part of the provisions at the common fire. The third cry sounds in the King's voice, but receives no answer."},"E218.2":{"s":"You go out to meet the third voice and find a golden cache near the old camp. The forest becomes silent for a moment.","f":"The third cry repeats the words of the King directly behind the party, and armed creatures emerge from the darkness. The battle begins."},"E218.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} sets up a patrol so that no one answers the third cry. In the morning, Dara supplies the party with supplies in gratitude.","f":"The third call causes one of the sentries to turn his head, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The third cry disrupts the patrol, but none of the eligible fighters is gravely wounded. You retreat behind the palisade for the night."}},"E218.4":{"s":"You leave camp before dark. The first child's cry comes from afar, and behind it comes Ock's familiar voice."},"E219.1":{"s":"You order the peasant to return Tilla's change, whether the buyer is alive or dead. The grateful skeleton rewards you with a sack of apples for the road."},"E219.2":{"s":"You pay Till three gold instead of the seller, and he carefully counts the coins with bone fingers. The argument by the road ends."},"E219.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} finds a simple answer in commercial law: the buyer is entitled to change, even if he dies. The peasant pays gold for legal clarification.","f":"{{heroName}} finds out that the dispute concerns the old law on dead buyers, and no one has the text of the law. The decision is postponed."},"E219.4":{"s":"You offer to leave the apples to Till and the money to the peasant, and both finally agree. As a thank you, you receive supplies.","f":"The peasant accuses Till of damaging the goods, and the skeleton takes out an old army sword. A skirmish begins."},"E220.1":{"s":"You acknowledge Ward's original bill of sale and reserve the place for the former owner. The skeleton pays gold for the restored right."},"E220.2":{"s":"You give Ward the gold for giving up the plot, and he signs the paper right on the lid of the coffin. A grateful Kessa gives the party supplies."},"E220.3":{"s":"You propose to dig up the adjacent grave, keeping the first one for Ward. The widow and skeleton agree, and the gravedigger gives supplies for resolving the dispute.","f":"Ward considers the neighboring grave to be a violation of the boundaries of his property and refuses the offer. Kessa continues to wait for the funeral."},"E220.4":{"s":"You do not interfere in the dispute between the owner of the grave and the new widow. The gravedigger again checks the original seal on the contract."}});
export { OUTCOMES_EN_E151_E220 };
